& [ArithmeticThreat]
  + ten names paired with count nine could permit omission of release or consumption while still claiming strict validation
  + mitigation is a constant ten-name sequence plus actual length declared count maximum equality and count-tamper adversary

& [CommissionThreats]
  + replay of a commission correlation or attempt can duplicate effects
  + self-issued subject identity can collapse operator and broker roles
  + stale carrier implementation bookend expected-current or plan digest can execute a superseded plan
  + scope alias parent traversal case drift or role overlap can widen mutation outside the intended scratch root
  + mitigation is exact identities distinct roles one attempt zero retries canonical paths strict descendants and domain digest

& [CapabilityThreats]
  + omitted denial unknown variant duplication reorder or overlap can widen future authority
  + requested future capability can be laundered into an issued current capability
  + mitigation is exact B0 declaration-order partition counts set equality aggregate digest and issued count zero

& [FenceThreats]
  + effect before claim enables replay while release before terminal publication creates concurrent mutation gaps
  + consumption before outcome loses recovery truth and cleanup after uncertainty erases evidence
  + stale lease recovery without owner evidence can steal a live commission
  + mitigation is ten exact steps continuous no-wait lease claim-before-effect publication-before-consumption consumption-before-release no retry and retained quarantine

& [InputThreats]
  + unknown duplicate over-depth oversize aliased rooted or parent-traversal artifact data can create parser disagreement
  + parsed-value-only verification can accept raw byte substitution
  + nondeterministic replay can hide state or ordering dependencies
  + mitigation is bounded raw identity strict serde duplicate preflight portable paths and byte-identical double replay

& [AuthorityThreats]
  + supplied authorization artifact may be mislabeled as authenticated consent
  + pure shape acceptance may be mislabeled as capacity or physical readiness
  + successful cached tests may be mislabeled as live provider or host execution
  + mitigation is commission_admission_only authority every physical boolean false explicit unresolved account and zero-effect counters

& [OperationalThreats]
  + low C-drive capacity and large rebuild caches can turn broad gates into host instability
  + WSL compaction cleanup remote fallback or policy bypass can exceed authority
  + mixed-ownership untracked enumeration can expose or absorb foreign work
  + mitigation is cached focused gates no cleanup no compaction no WSL compile no remote fallback no host-policy weakening and tracked-plus-explicit attribution

& [Residual]
  + production commission authentication current clock lease ledger process containment recovery and physical evidence remain unsolved
  + P1 SWA-06B persistence and activation remain downstream gates
